= LPS Common Library Software Release Procedure

= Tool Information

.Summary Of Tools Used
 - Git:            MSysGit 1.9.4 (Preview 2014-09-29) For Windows
 - Ivy Utilities:  12.6.1
 - Electric Make:  7.1.4.52942 32-bit (build_7.1_52942_OPT_2014.04.25_08:09:18)

NOTE:  All other tools are called out under version control.

== Release Procedure

.Process
 1) Do software changes.
 2) Test it to insure that it works.
 3) Make sure to update any external dependancies in the Ivy file.
    Update "deps/ivy.xml" to reference any lower level libraries
    or tools used by this release unit.
 4) Change directory to the repository area under the Ivy view with the desired
    content to be released.
    e.g.
        (100)% cd /c/users/<cwsid>/ivy/<view>/lib/lib_mach_productivity/lps/lps_common
 5) Ensure that all content has been commited.
    If any files are reported, then the release should not go forward
    until it is resolved.
    e.g.
        (101)% git status --untracked
        # On branch master
        nothing to commit, working directory clean
 6) Tag repository with new release version.
    IMP NOTE: replace release tag before publish descriptor.
    e.g.	    
		(102)% git tag -m "New release." 0.1.0
		
 7) Push tag (and commit if it has not already been synched) to server.
    e.g.       
		(103)% git push --tags origin master				
		
 8) Update release computer's Ivy Dependancy database.
    e.g.
        (104)% ivyu project --install
 9) Create Ivy Descriptor for new release, and publish it locally to
    release computer's ivy-xml resolver.
	IMP NOTE: replace release tag before publish descriptor.
    e.g.   	
		(105)% ivyu --descriptor cat/ess-info/lps_common TBD pubFR --ivyoffset deps --tag 0.1.0
				
10) Ensure that Ivy Domain for new release only contains newly released
    descriptor.
    e.g.
        (106)% cd /c/users/<cwsid>/ivy/ivy-xml/ivy-mach_productivity/
        (107)% git status --untracked
      
11) Add new Ivy descriptor for this release to Ivy Dependancy repository.
    e.g.
        (108)% git add --all
        (109)% git commit -m "Release Ivy Descriptors for new release."
12) Push commit of Ivy descriptor for this release to public repository.
    e.g.
        (110)% git push origin master
